 "caption": "He just wanted to say hello. Hell said it back, louder. Sick Of It. #SickOfIt #pixelart #indiegame #comedy #hawkesgen hawkesgen.com",
 "summary": "v5, answering Studio's review of v4. Cause of the audio slip: the upscaled clips still carried the sound baked into the lipsync/i2v renders (the hero's Nope, Yooba's mumble, stray voices) and video.compose mixed it under the placed tracks. Every clip is now sound:false, so only the placed table-read stems, SFX and drone play. Per note: (1) 0:16 Hell's HELLO over Nope: placed Hell echo 3 stays at 12.84 (fire column) and Nope at 16.24; the baked clip audio that overlapped is gone. (2) 0:21 hero voice over Yooba: removed with the baked audio; only Yooba's stem plays at 21.38. (3) 0:27 Yooba line in Hell: removed; only the announcer plays. (4) 0:29 announcer cut: it runs 27.09-29.49, ends before the end card at 29.96, no clip audio competes. (5) 0:17 suction stepped: FILM x2 interpolation of the suck clip queued (j_0c50ca69e0fc); it will be swapped in when done. Critic not run (Gemini quota earlier); loudness-per-0.5s checked against the placed times."
